@inject TileArt Art

@* The match page's Help view: what doesn't need to be on the main screen every round (owner's choice, 24 Oct 2026).
   Your trait's goal, the tile types, the opening, a round, and scoring. *@

@{
    var match = Match;
    var me = match.Seats[You];
}
    <div class="match-help">
    <h2 class="h4">How to play</h2>

    @if (me.Trait is { } trait)
    {
        <h2 class="h4">Your trait: @trait</h2>
        <p>@Capitalised(match.GoalText(trait).TrimEnd('.')). Rivals learn it only when the match ends, and you learn theirs.</p>
    }

    <h2 class="h4">Tiles</h2>
    <ul class="help-list">
        @foreach (var type in Enum.GetValues<TileType>())
        {
            <li>
                @if (Art.Paths is { } art)
                {
                    <img class="tile-swatch" src="@Assets[art[type]]" alt="" />
                }
                <span class="tile-mark">@Seats.Mark(type)</span>
                <b>@type</b>: @(match.Rules.Varies(type) ? $"rolls {match.Rules.YieldRange(type)} mana each round" : $"yields {match.Rules.YieldRange(type)} mana every round").
            </li>
        }
    </ul>
    <p><ManaIcon /> is mana. A held tile shows what it paid this round (<span class="text-nowrap">"+3 <ManaIcon />").</span> Monsters (☠) guard some tiles revealed later; beat them to take
        the tile.</p>

    <h2 class="h4">The opening</h2>
    <p>@match.Rules.OpeningUnveils drafts each reveal one tile per player, and everyone takes one in turn, for free. The
        first draft starts with seat 1, the next one seat later, and so on; the last to pick gets the tile left over.</p>

    <h2 class="h4">A round</h2>
    <p>Everyone picks one stance in secret, then all resolve together:</p>
    <ul class="help-list">
        <li><b>Attune</b>: claim a free tile next to your land.</li>
        <li><b>Summon</b>: put Imps (power @match.Rules.ImpPower, @match.Rules.ImpCost mana) or Golems (power
            @match.Rules.GolemPower, @match.Rules.GolemCost mana, upkeep @match.Rules.GolemUpkeep) on one of your tiles.</li>
        <li><b>Attack</b>: send units at a rival's or a monster's tile next to them.</li>
        <li><b>Build</b>: an upgrade on one of your tiles.</li>
        <li><b>Hold</b>: do nothing.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Units can also step between your neighbouring tiles first, and one spell a round goes alongside the stance. A
        stance nobody chose gets cheaper the next round.</p>

    <h2 class="h4">Scoring</h2>
    <p>Every round you bank points for your land and your mana income, and for tiles you take. At the end, upgrades and
        your trait's goal add theirs. After @match.Rules.Rounds rounds, the most points wins.</p>

    <h2 class="h4">Every trait</h2>
    <ul class="help-list">
        @foreach (var t in Enum.GetValues<Trait>())
        {
            <li><b>@t</b>: @match.GoalText(t)</li>
        }
    </ul>
    </div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public Match Match { get; set; } = default!;

    [Parameter]
    public int You { get; set; }

    private static string Capitalised(string text) => text.Length == 0 ? text : char.ToUpperInvariant(text[0]) + text[1..];
}
